
SonarQube & Vulnerability Prevention

SonarQube is an open-source static application security testing (SAST) platform used for continuous inspection of code quality. It scans source code to detect bugs, code smells, security vulnerabilities, and security hotspots across 30+ programming languages.
To prevent vulnerabilities in both code and dependencies, developers combine SonarQube with dependency scanning tools:
• Code Vulnerabilities (SAST): SonarQube integrates into the CI/CD pipeline (e.g., Jenkins, GitHub Actions). It enforces Quality Gates that block code from merging if it contains critical vulnerabilities, security hotspots, or insufficient unit test coverage.
• Dependency Vulnerabilities (SCA): SonarQube primarily checks your custom source code. To find vulnerabilities in third-party libraries (like transitive dependencies), it is paired with Software Composition Analysis (SCA) tools like OWASP Dependency-Check, Snyk, or GitHub Dependabot. These tools scan pom.xml or build.gradle against known CVE databases.

