You can customize Spring Boot's auto-configuration settings by defining key-value pairs inside the src/main/resources/application.properties file.
Spring Boot provides thousands of built-in configuration keys. When you define a key in this file, Spring Boot detects it at startup and uses your custom value instead of its default choice.
Here is a grouped checklist of the most common auto-configuration overrides used in development.

1. Server Customization

By default, Spring Boot starts an embedded Tomcat server on port 8080 with a root context path (/). You can change this behavior instantly:
